{"availability":"available","full":"block/trailblaze","name":"trailblaze","description":"🥾 AI-Driven UI Testing Framework with Recorded Trails","category":"Developer tools","language":"Kotlin","stars":321,"forks":31,"created":"2025-06-10T18:29:40Z","updated":"2026-10-06T12:08:40Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://block.github.io/trailblaze/","topics":[],"demo":"https://block.github.io/trailblaze/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.321Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.321Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.321Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.321Z","stars":321,"forks":31}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Natural-language device control for your coding agent — across iOS, Android, and web. Every session is a replayable trail you can run as a test.","Point your coding agent — Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Goose — at the trailblaze CLI and it can read any screen and act on it, on a real device. Save the session and you have a trail — one trail.yaml holding natural-language steps your team reads and recorded actions your CI replays deterministically — no LLM at replay time."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/block/trailblaze/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3d958531062502cbd8356c20a38bbb89faf8a48c7bb84c19c7b217a8e3e4b391","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.623Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:52.623Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Natural-language device control for your coding agent — across iOS, Android, and web. Every session is a replayable trail you can run as a test.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/block/trailblaze/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Android, and web — built-in primitives plus first-class custom commands like login or addToCart that you define in TypeScript with typed inputs and IDE support.","sourceUrl":"https://github.c